@startuml
title A deliberately simple layer stack for a first protocol

rectangle "Application handlers" as L1
rectangle "Request / notification dispatcher" as L2
rectangle "Pending-request manager" as L3
rectangle "Encoder / decoder" as L4
rectangle "Framing and validation" as L5
rectangle "Single TX queue + RX parser" as L6
rectangle "UART / USB CDC / TCP / WebSocket" as L7

L1 --> L2
L2 --> L3
L3 --> L4
L4 --> L5
L5 --> L6
L6 --> L7

note right of L3
  Each layer only knows the one below it,
  so a transport can be swapped without
  touching the handlers.
end note
@enduml
